<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alimirah Hanfare</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1922–<a href="/years/2011">2011</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alimirah Hanfare was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aussa">Aussa</a>, the traditional leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, from 1944 until his death in 2011. He resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> military government after 1975 and went into exile in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, while the Afar Liberation Front, led by his family, fought the regime. He returned in 1991 and remained a central figure in Afar regional politics.</p></div>
